  "result": "Fixed. `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:33` matched lines by `l.item.name` when it should have matched by `l.item.sku`. Calling `remove('sku-1')` compared `'sku-1'` with the name `'Widget'`, found no match, and left the line in the cart. `Cart.add` already matches by SKU, so I changed `remove` to do the same.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1` (only the Gadget is left). Before the fix the Widget line stayed in the cart.\n- I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest`, since pytest isn't installed here: all 6 pass.\n\nNone of the existing tests call `Cart.remove`, which is how this bug got through. I can add a regression test for it if you'd like.",
